# R session droppings
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.RDataTmp*
.Rapp.history

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Pitch data is rebuildable from the daily chain and runs to tens of MB.
*.rds

# data/ holds the two artifacts the app reads at startup, both rebuilt by
# scripts/update_data.R. The two-line form is required: a bare `data/` ignores
# the directory itself, so git never descends into it and the negation below
# could never re-include anything.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# The regression fixtures are TRACKED, both of them, 217 KB together.
# tests/fixtures/pl_trim_702070.rds is the frozen input phase1_check.R compares
# both sides against, and arsenal_gt_null_baseline.rds is a byte snapshot of the
# table that fixture renders. Gitignored, they regenerated on every clone off a
# season store that grows nightly: the fixture went 2,261 to 2,346 pitches
# between 2026-08-19 and 2026-08-23, at which point the byte-identity baseline
# compares two different tables and means nothing. Frozen files are only frozen
# if they are committed.
!tests/fixtures/*.rds

# Chain run log, machine-local
logs/
